    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1805.06507v2</id>
    <title>Nowhere-differentiability of the solution map of 2D Euler equations on bounded spatial domain</title>
    <updated>2019-06-26T19:41:18Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.06507v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1805.06507v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We consider the incompressible 2D Euler equations on bounded spatial domain $S$, and study the solution map on the Sobolev spaces $H^k(S)$ ($k &gt; 2$). Through an elaborate geometric construction, we show that for any $T &gt;0$, the time $T$ solution map $u_0 \mapsto u(T)$ is nowhere locally uniformly continuous and nowhere Fréchet differentiable.</summary>
